{"t": 1794117526.8018873, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Regression alert: this change introduced a production reconciliation bug.\n\nSentry issue: https://sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/ \u2014 **ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit** (expected 1100, got 1099). First seen in release `ledger-worker@2026.11.3`, 2,201 events, still unresolved.\n\nRoot cause: `worker/rates.py` now truncates with `int(amount_minor * rate)` instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, so fractional minor units are dropped (e.g. 1099.9 -> 1099 instead of 1100). I've restored rounding in `worker/rates.py`. Please avoid replacing it with truncation for speed.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
